  ('2cd5e3c6-a8c0-456a-ab47-5e7b3a435407', 'Reverse Curl', 'Biceps, Brachialis', 'The reverse-grip barbell curl is a variation on the biceps curl where the palms face downward. The switch from an underhand to an overhand grip brings the forearm and brachialis muscles more into the exercise.', 'Barbell, Dumbbell', 'wger', 'CC0', 'BFad07', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/495/view/'),
  ('960697af-9a0e-4bfd-a8ba-989718b6b5c7', 'Reverse EZ Bar Cable Curls', 'Biceps', 'Standing in front of cable tower using a SZ Bar', 'Cable machine, SZ-Bar', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'novadani', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/914/view/'),
  ('440cf10c-effb-4b63-a6e0-182fe47376f6', 'Reverse Fly Standing', 'Shoulders, Trapezius', '- Stand with a good posture holding a cable in each hand opposite the machine
- Starting with the hands in front of your chest pull the arms out to
your side into the shape of a T with the elbows nearly straight
- Slowly release the arms forward to the start
- Repeat with the arms moving into the shape of a Y
- Repeat with the arms in the shape of a W
- Repeat with the arms in the shape of an L by your side', 'Cable machine', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'Croak6728', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1709/view/'),
  ('dd6e8753-a574-476e-900a-b794eb592e7b', 'Reverse Grip Barbell Curls', 'Biceps', 'Hold the barbell with an overhand grip (palms facing down) approximately shoulder-width apart. Ensure your back is straight, shoulders slightly pulled back, and arms fully extended.
Curl the barbell upwards towards your chest in a controlled motion, keeping your elbows close to your body. The motion should be smooth without any swinging or momentum use.
Once the barbell is at chest level, pause briefly to maximize contraction in the biceps and forearms.
Slowly lower the barbell back to the starting position with a controlled movement, fully extending your arms.', 'Barbell', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'sTiKyt', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1290/view/'),
  ('1b95d961-1d5c-4ded-b25e-c090295ffe37', 'Reverse Grip Bench Press', 'Chest, Triceps', 'Upper chest focuses exercise that also works triceps', 'Barbell, Bench', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'bl0sh', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/498/view/'),
  ('682ea312-af02-450a-9880-fea7bf8e854a', 'Reverse Hyperextension', 'Hamstrings, Glutes', 'Lie face-down on a bench with your legs hanging off the edge.
- Bend your hips so your thighs are vertical, bending your knees at the same time so your shins stay horizontal.
- Straighten out your legs so they are not bent and your toes are pointing backwards horizontally.
- Return to the original position, and repeat.', 'Bench', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'Croak6728', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1809/view/'),
  ('616f9026-1a1d-4ed8-b068-cfbb81b6a000', 'Reverse lunges', 'Glutes, Quads', 'Starting position:
Stand straight, feet hip-width apart.
Steps:
- Step backward with one leg so it can bend comfortably to a 90 degree angle.
- Slowly bend both knees to form 90 degree angles.
- Return to the starting position.
- Repeat, alternating legs.', 'none (bodyweight exercise)', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', null, 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/999/view/'),
  ('6cbdd70c-0691-4288-b58a-24001384f1b3', 'Reverse Nordic Curl', 'Quads', 'Natural Leg Extension is alternative to Leg Extension machine with no equipment.', null, 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'karly', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/909/view/'),
  ('09349391-375b-42d5-8979-00a5d7196a5b', 'Reverse Plank', null, 'Plank with stomach towards ceiling', 'none (bodyweight exercise)', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'spacetowaste', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/500/view/'),
  ('edc44b1a-35d7-4c37-ab20-05842fb40576', 'Reverse Preacher Curl (Close Grip)', 'Biceps', 'Sitting reverse on a Biceps Bench with a close grip', 'SZ-Bar', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'novadani', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/913/view/'),
  ('603895ca-20a0-4272-a62b-293d14220390', 'Reverse Snow Angel', 'Trapezius', 'Lay flat on your stomach with your arms extended in front of you on the ground as your legs are lying flat. Lift both your arms and move them to your side slowly. Then, move them back.', 'none (bodyweight exercise)', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'mike6426', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1215/view/'),
  ('04063ba5-05d1-48b9-9571-eae2b8edab29', 'Reverse V-Squat', 'Glutes, Quads', 'Step into the V-squat machine facing the pad, the opposite way from the regular V-squat, so that your chest rests against the pad and your shoulders sit under the shoulder pads. Place your feet on the platform about shoulder width apart and release the safety.
Brace your core and lower yourself by bending your knees and pushing the hips back until your thighs are roughly parallel to the platform. Drive back up through the heels without locking out the knees.
Compared to the regular V-squat, the reversed position shifts the emphasis towards the glutes and hamstrings.', null, 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'aboksz', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/2620/view/'),
  ('6f5d4373-66d1-4acd-a16f-ba0e636fe979', 'Reverse Wood Chops', 'Glutes, Lats', '- Attach a looping resistance band to a rack below knee height
- Grip the other end of the band like holding a baseball bat with both hands
- Stretch the band facing it
- Start with your hands at the side of your hips, knees bent
- Rotate your hips while moving your hands towards over the top of your opposite shoulder
- Imagine the motion as striking a baseball with a bat', 'none (bodyweight exercise)', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'M9', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1433/view/'),
  ('2acb5ba1-caa3-4204-9903-ff0095b032ba', 'Reverse-grip pull-ups', 'Biceps, Lats', 'Pull-ups on the bar with your thumbs pointing outward.', 'Pull-up bar', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'clafal', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1292/view/'),
  ('6f6f4269-113e-4e20-a18c-1d09adad8d0d', 'Rice Bucket Training', null, 'Fill a deep bucket with dry rice. Push your hand into the rice and repeatedly open and close your fist, twist your wrist both ways, and spread your fingers against the rice for the set time. This is a low impact way to train every muscle of the hand and forearm and is good for warming up or recovery.', null, 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'lightking', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/2745/view/'),
  ('8374a856-9293-4b90-900e-00c3bfe21cc4', 'Right levator scapulae stretch', null, 'Starting position:
Start standing up or sitting down. Turn your head to the right, around 45 degrees or just above your nipple. Place your left hand behind your back or sit on it. Take your right hand and use it to hold the back of your head. Lean your head down slightly.
Steps:
- After assuming the starting position, press your head against your right hand with slight force. Your hand should press back with equal force, so that your head doesn''t move. Hold this position.', 'none (bodyweight exercise)', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', null, 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1014/view/'),
  ('7ea504e7-3310-4638-a111-054fabfd4b80', 'Right neck stretch', null, 'Starting position:
Sit or stand with your back straight.
Steps:
- Tilt your head to the side.
- Take the hand closer to your head and use it to grab your head from the other side.
- Push with your hand against your head and with your head against your hand so that the forces balance out and your head stays still.
- Maintain this tension until the end of the exercise.', 'none (bodyweight exercise)', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', null, 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1009/view/'),
  ('7671b16c-5023-4663-b00d-86dd018e024f', 'Ring Dips', 'Triceps', 'Dips peformed on gymnastic rings.', null, 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'Nash', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/501/view/'),
  ('6c9c9d14-e6bf-43ed-9859-a689e2131fe0', 'Ring Support Hold', null, 'Hold yourself in a support position on gymnastic rings with arms straight at sides. Focus on keeping rings turned out slightly and maintaining hollow body position. This is an isometric hold for chest, shoulders, and triceps.', null, 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', null, 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1832/view/'),
  ('0dfe655e-ee2e-4c49-a279-c672d5591613', 'Rocking Triceps Pushdown', 'Triceps', 'Set your feet below the rope and lean your upper body towards the rope. Set one foot back. Push down the rope and lean your entire body back onto the rear foot as you push down to get your hands behind your body. Don''t forget to bring your chest to the front during the pushdown. As you release the rope slowly, lean your body back onto the front foot.', 'Cable machine, SZ-Bar', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'Moffi', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1485/view/'),
  ('d5ee3b1f-2879-406f-97a9-51a8b0817cd4', 'Roll Down', null, 'Stand with your feet hip-width apart and slowly roll your upper body forward, one vertebra at a time, until your hands touch the ground or as far as you can comfortably go. Roll back up to the starting position in the same controlled manner.', 'none (bodyweight exercise)', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'captive0592', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1399/view/'),
  ('752c0380-a0f9-4332-8265-cf503bac4703', 'Roll-overs into V-sits', null, 'Roll-overs into V-sits
Part of: Limber 11
Source: Joe DeFranco
Prescription: 10 reps
Type: dynamic', null, 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'Pete-E automation', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1954/view/'),
  ('af2f774c-296c-4d14-8e4a-fad77175ae37', 'Roman Chair Crunch', 'Abs', 'Crunches on roman chair. Keep your torso straight, abs tight, and don''t come up all the way vertical or lie flat to keep constant tension on your abs.', null, 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 3', 'MaddieBeasley', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/505/view/'),
  ('2e7ffff9-e603-4b28-98c8-31d1a6ce8cd9', 'Romanian Deadlift', 'Hamstrings, Glutes', 'DL from top to pos 2: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WtWtjViRsKo', 'Barbell', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'pjwirth', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/507/view/'),
  ('ef86d3ad-a57c-4eb3-98d6-e023ab4b842f', 'Romanian Deadlift (Custom)', 'Hamstrings, Glutes', 'Perform Romanian Deadlift with controlled form, keeping tension on the target muscles, pausing briefly at the peak contraction, then returning slowly under control without using momentum.', 'Barbell', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'ruochenma', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/2710/view/'),
  ('b5df1592-d055-4e3f-a070-f12904d7c72e', 'Rope Climb', 'Lats', 'Grip a hanging climbing rope with both hands overhead. Pull yourself up hand over hand, using your legs to clamp the rope if needed, then climb down with control. Beginners can start seated on the floor and pull up to standing. This builds pulling and grip strength together.', null, 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'lightking', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/2747/view/'),
  ('148f2ffc-05e2-486b-874f-2a401337a1c6', 'Rope Pullover/row', 'Lats', 'Set up bench in front of cable row machine. Lean over bench to do a row/pullover with rope that targets lats. See picture.', 'Cable machine, Incline bench', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'Rottekongen', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1634/view/'),
  ('849f2fa6-42f9-4c59-90f6-275c8ada6725', 'Rotary Torso Machine', 'Abs', '- Slow and Steady
- Not too much weight', null, 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', '6LXBO', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1374/view/'),
  ('4b7cb037-0789-4014-ab6f-a451716b7538', 'Row', 'Lats, Trapezius', 'In strength training, rowing (or a row, usually preceded by a qualifying adjective — for instance a seated row) is an exercise where the purpose is to strengthen the muscles that draw the rower''s arms toward the body (latissimus dorsi) as well as those that retract the scapulae (trapezius and rhomboids) and those that support the spine (erector spinae). When done on a rowing machine, rowing also exercises muscles that extend and support the legs (quadriceps and thigh muscles). In all cases, the abdominal and lower back muscles must be used in order to support the body and prevent back injury.', 'Barbell, Dumbbell, Pull-up bar', 'wger', 'CC0', 'BFad07', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/508/view/'),
  ('f6d8e157-c233-4a22-9c1a-83cb8f613ea5', 'Rowing Machine', 'Shoulders, Biceps, Hamstrings, Brachialis, Calves, Glutes, Lats, Obliquus externus abdominis, Quads, Abs, Serratus anterior, Soleus, Trapezius', 'Sit on a rowing machine with your back straight.', 'none (bodyweight exercise)', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'Boertie', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1093/view/'),
  ('00fcf603-b0d0-48d2-9b5e-c7f0d510d46c', 'Rowing seated, narrow grip', 'Lats', '- Tighten muscles
- Controlled movement
- Slow movement
- Keep upper body upright
- Do not lean back
- Pull toward chest', null, 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 3', 'wger.de', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/512/view/'),
  ('8766d43c-e035-4c37-b824-b94dce5bf710', 'Rowing with TRX band', 'Lats', 'Rowing with resistance bands - Bodyweight Exercise', 'none (bodyweight exercise)', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'Skadi', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/674/view/'),
  ('88dbcc74-0304-4fcf-8a47-92d14a484b0a', 'Rowing, Lying on Bench', 'Lats', null, null, 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 3', 'wger.de', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/510/view/'),
  ('32c129f7-cc28-4ebc-8465-e4fa62e220b1', 'Rowing, T-bar', 'Lats', 'The execution of this exercise is very similar to the regular bent over rowing, only that the bar is fixed here.
Grab the barbell with a wide grip (slightly more than shoulder wide) and lean forward. Your upper body is not quite parallel to the floor, but forms a slight angle. The chest''s out during the whole exercise. Pull now the barbell with a fast movement towards your belly button, not further up. Go slowly down to the initial position. Don''t swing with your body and keep your arms next to your body.', null, 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 3', 'wger.de', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/513/view/'),
  ('4221c8af-b3ca-4a53-9176-bd66e46d10f2', 'rubber band glute kickback', 'Glutes', 'A rubber band glute kickback is an exercise performed on hands and knees, where you anchor a resistance band to your foot and kick your heel back and up, squeezing your glute at the top of the movement, while maintaining a stable core and flat back to target and strengthen the gluteal muscles.', 'Resistance band', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'Tierrasverdes', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1613/view/'),
  ('a48295d8-21da-4625-8a85-331d7ced8d8b', 'Run', null, 'Running or jogging outside in a park, on the tracks,...', 'none (bodyweight exercise)', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'BeLikeWater', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/527/view/'),
  ('6cf55ecc-86ee-492d-a7f6-977bf61758b3', 'Run - Interval Training', null, 'Run and do some interval trainings such as hill repat, fartlek,..', 'none (bodyweight exercise)', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'BeLikeWater', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/529/view/'),
  ('654793c2-e0e3-41fd-a549-0ece0f4378e8', 'Run - Treadmill', null, 'Run on a treadmill', null, 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 3', 'foguinho.peruca', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/530/view/'),
  ('92cd0459-5cd1-46a0-934d-e7cff8d4ccda', 'Runners Lunge Stretch', null, 'View the video to undestand the exercise', 'none (bodyweight exercise)', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'Davidgj32', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1874/view/'),
  ('58ba2ce1-c140-4a9f-9bbc-d99776909690', 'Russian Push Ups', 'Chest', 'Russian Push-Ups
Start in a standard push-up position with your hands slightly wider than shoulder-width apart. Lower your chest toward the floor, then shift your body forward while keeping your chest close to the ground. Extend your arms to return to the starting position, then reverse the movement smoothly. Keep your core tight and maintain controlled movement throughout the exercise.', 'none (bodyweight exercise)', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'ege', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/2530/view/'),
  ('10510fb5-6ebd-4ddc-b03e-423b15deceea', 'Russian Twist', 'Lats, Obliquus externus abdominis, Abs', '- Hold a dumbbell, barbell weight or something else that is heavy with both hands, but make sure it is not too heavy and you are able to keep in form.
- Lean back to a 45-degree angle from the floor. For an extra challenge, lift your feet off the floor.
- Rotate your arms to one side to the same level as your chest, touch the floor for a little extra challenge, and then do the same to the other side. When you''re back in your original position after doing both sides it will count as 1 rep.', 'Dumbbell, Gym mat, Swiss Ball', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'lion', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1193/view/'),
  ('2a983b8f-b77e-4f8f-8335-0e5caecd715f', 'Scapula Pulls', 'Lats, Trapezius', '- Hang straight on a pull-up bar
- Pull shoulder blades together, moving the body slightly up', 'Pull-up bar', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'M9', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1435/view/'),
  ('e044cd7d-ef86-4154-a3a8-bd01fc5535ab', 'Scapular Pushups', 'Serratus anterior', 'Start in a straight-arm plank with your hands under your shoulders. Keep your elbows locked and move only your shoulder blades: let your chest sink slightly, then push the floor away to spread the shoulder blades. Move in a comfortable, controlled range.', 'none (bodyweight exercise)', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'nalhilal', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/2681/view/'),
  ('f5252c85-04b7-48f0-97cf-711f326a5821', 'Schwimmen', null, '- 800m Schwimmen in 20 Minuten', null, 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'delta@romeo', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1574/view/'),
  ('e28b0685-7a8f-4343-9c0b-63b38386d30b', 'Scissors', 'Abs', 'Scissors is an abdominal exercise that strengthens the transverse abdominals, helping flatten your belly and strengthen your entire core. Scissors is not only a core strength move, but it is also a great stretch for your hamstrings and your lower back. Everyone is looking for new ways to work the core, to flatten the belly and to improve flexibility. If you learn how to do Scissors you will get everything rolled together in one move.', null, 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'vkylamba', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/545/view/'),
  ('89651d40-9abf-49b5-9ee5-7b0ecb25fd03', 'Scorpion Kick', null, 'Get into the push-up position with your shoulders directly above your hands and your feet hip-width apart.
Make sure that your body forms a straight line from your head to your heels.
Now pull your right knee towards your chest. While keeping your knee bent, lift your right leg as high as possible with your lower right leg pointing straight up.
Now rotate your hips so that your right foot swings over your left leg.
Continue to rotate and move your right foot towards the floor until you are forced to roll onto the outside of your left standing foot. Make sure that you do not rotate your upper body.
Now return to the starting position and repeat the exercise with your left leg.', 'none (bodyweight exercise)', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'lxmx', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1207/view/'),
  ('deebd257-f84d-4879-9dc4-353ee0ea534f', 'Seated Back Extension Machine', 'Lats, Serratus anterior', '- Adjust the seat and the back pad so that the pad sits at the height of your shoulder blades or mid-back.
- Sit in the machine with your hips and lower back against the seat and backrest and your feet on the platform. Cross your arms over your chest or hold the handles.
- Exhale and push the pad backwards using your lower back muscles until your spine is in line with your hips. Pause for a second at the end position.
- Inhale and slowly return to the starting position, without letting the weight stack slam down.', null, 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'Franpol', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1143/view/'),
  ('6b6bd3ce-c40d-486c-9c47-21a3c639626d', 'Seated Band Row', 'Lats', 'Sit on the floor with your legs straight out in front of you and your back tall. Loop a resistance band around the soles of both feet and hold one end in each hand, arms extended and a slight bend in the knees. Pull the band toward your lower ribs by driving your elbows straight back and squeezing your shoulder blades together. Keep your chest up and your torso still rather than rocking backward to move the band. Extend the arms slowly to return. Because the torso stays upright and supported, this is a useful row when a bent-over position is uncomfortable, and it needs no anchor point.', 'Resistance band', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'trs1800', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/2635/view/'),
  ('117df66c-bc8d-43cc-9903-0be2a0864486', 'Seated Bench Press', 'Chest', 'Set up the chest press machine so that the grips are aligned with your lower chest when you sit down. Make sure you''re sitting with your back flat against the seat. Grab a handle in each hand, stick your chest out, and keep your head against the headrest. Breathe deeply and slowly push the handles forward until your arms are almost fully extended. Pause just before the lockout, then slowly return the handles to the starting position. Pause just before the handles come to a complete stop and perform another repetition.', 'Bench', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'colundrum', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1094/view/'),
  ('139772c6-e401-4281-8aa6-c7ff7fb49f6a', 'Seated Cable chest fly', 'Chest', '- Place a bench between two cable pulleys and adjust the pulleys so they are at chest/shoulder height when you are seated.
- Grab the handles with a neutral grip and lean against the upright backrest.
- Bring your arms together in front of your chest in a controlled motion, focusing on squeezing your chest muscles. Keep your elbows slightly bent throughout the movement.
- Pause briefly at the top position.
- Slowly lower your arms back to the starting position while maintaining control of the movement.
- Repeat for reps.', 'Cable machine', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'shushu', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1922/view/'),
  ('ad3716b1-5fc9-45aa-9de4-9a1c0153915d', 'Seated Cable Mid Trap Shrug', 'Trapezius', 'seated straight back, slight hold at top', 'Cable machine', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'novadani', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/922/view/'),
  ('0ecfec6f-5d0f-4e8a-8d37-f6203a8923b8', 'Seated Cable Row', 'Lats', '- Take a seat on the machine with your feet planted, a little wider than shoulder width. Drive the heels, and squeeze the glutes. Grab onto the cable handle.
- Sit up tall with a slight bend through the knees. Tighten up the abs and low back to maintain a perpendicular angle to the floor with your torso.
- Roll the shoulders back and down. Squeeze them together as you row, thinking about pinching a pencil in between them. As you do this, pull the handle back towards you, landing right above your belly button.
- Pause here for a moment before returning the handle, still squeezing the shoulder blades. Once you''ve returned the weight to the stack, then allow the shoulder blades to relax, without pulling the torso forward.
- Repeat the movement.', 'Cable machine', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'Franpol', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1117/view/'),
  ('e9891a94-b1d4-47f4-a82b-c1aa82121abb', 'Seated Corkscrew', 'Obliquus externus abdominis, Abs', 'To
do this abs and obliques exercise, start with your hands back behind your body
and bring your knees in and across, really trying to contract the obliques.
Then extend your legs back out to starting position and repeat toward the
opposite side of the abs.
Beginners
might find that they can’t even get through the first 45 seconds of this
challenging reverse crunches variation.  That’s ok because it gives you a
place to start and something to improve upon.', 'none (bodyweight exercise)', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'Moffi', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1477/view/'),
  ('ed504e06-a14b-4550-b31b-4fcbbd2009e3', 'Seated Dumbbell Biceps Curl (Custom)', 'Biceps', 'Sit with your back supported, keep the upper arms fixed at your sides, curl the dumbbells up, pause briefly at the top, lower slowly under control without swinging the back.', 'Dumbbell', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'ruochenma', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/2755/view/'),
  ('6995c30a-037f-4de3-ac4a-45384a1f38f9', 'Seated Dumbbell Calf Raise', 'Calves', 'The seated dumbbell calf raise is a targeted exercise for strengthening the lower leg muscles. It follows the same movement pattern as the machine version: you place the weight on your knees, and by extending and flexing your ankles, you move the weight.', 'Dumbbell', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'AlucardEvil40', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1620/view/'),
  ('19fba43a-8363-4da3-82c6-d8a14628b5e7', 'Seated Dumbbell Curls', 'Biceps', 'Seated Dumbbell Curls are an effective bicep workout that isolates the muscles by stabilizing the upper body, reducing momentum that can detract from the exercise’s effectiveness. This exercise is performed sitting down with a dumbbell in each hand, focusing on controlled movement to maximize engagement of the bicep muscles.', 'Dumbbell', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'sTiKyt', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1289/view/'),
  ('6d010eae-2e36-4ec6-b191-c0373f237bb4', 'Seated Dumbbell Side Lateral', 'Shoulders', 'seated slightly leaned forward at beginning of exercise', 'Dumbbell', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'novadani', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/918/view/'),
  ('6d4f77b5-ac3b-4299-b6aa-ff774250a627', 'Seated Dumbbell Side Lateral (Custom)', 'Shoulders', 'Perform Seated Dumbbell Side Lateral with controlled form, keeping tension on the target muscles, pausing briefly at the peak contraction, then returning slowly under control without using momentum.', 'Dumbbell', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'ruochenma', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/2714/view/'),
  ('73144238-414e-438f-8b0c-832a6591aa2f', 'seated figure four', 'Glutes', 'Seat on  a bench. Feet flat on the ground. Place your left ankle over your right knee. Your right knee stays flat. Keep your back straight. Gently push your left knee down.', 'Bench', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'ricardodavidrd', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1680/view/'),
  ('b144ac00-ec0c-4c43-898f-b2ac65048d98', 'Seated Hip Abduction', 'Glutes', 'Starting Position:
- Adjust the seat height so that your knees are aligned with the pivot point of the machine.
- Sit with your back flat against the backrest, maintaining good posture.
- Place the outside of your thighs against the machine''s padded levers.
- Position your feet flat on the footrests or platform of the machine.
- Grasp the handles or sides of the seat for stability.
- Ensure your spine is neutral and your core is slightly engaged.
Movement:
- Exhale as you slowly push your legs outward against the resistance pads.
- Focus on initiating the movement from your hips, not your knees.
- Continue opening your legs until you feel a strong contraction in your outer hips and thighs.
- Hold the fully abducted position briefly (1-2 seconds) to maximize muscle engagement.
- Inhale as you slowly control the return of your legs to the starting position, resisting the weight throughout the movement.
- Avoid allowing the weight stack to touch down between repetitions to maintain constant tension on the muscles.
- Repeat for the desired number of repetitions, maintaining control throughout the set.', 'none (bodyweight exercise)', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'Iko', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1672/view/'),
  ('5626ef93-290e-4f55-9113-6d66d56a2440', 'Seated Hip Abduction (Custom)', 'Glutes', 'Perform Seated Hip Abduction with controlled form, keeping tension on the target muscles, pausing briefly at the peak contraction, then returning slowly under control without using momentum.', 'none (bodyweight exercise)', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'ruochenma', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/2718/view/'),
  ('53906cd1-61f1-4d56-ac60-e4fcc5824861', 'Seated Hip Adduction', 'Glutes', 'Starting Position: Sit on the machine with your knees inward and against the pads. Pull the pin to release the pads. Grab the handles on the sides.b', null, 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 3', 'flori', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/12/view/'),
  ('9926363e-3db6-4f40-b830-589758bb79e0', 'Seated Hip Adduction (Custom)', 'Glutes', 'Sit on the machine with your back against the pad, place the insides of your legs against the pads, squeeze your inner thighs together, pause briefly, then return slowly under control.', null, 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'ruochenma', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/2699/view/'),
  ('a3afaf43-b087-4f65-9e62-d038ab09ce90', 'Seated Knee Extension with Overpressure', 'Hamstrings', 'A gentle stretch to restore full knee extension. Sit with one leg stretched out in front of you and the heel propped on the floor or a low surface, so the knee is unsupported. Place both hands on the thigh just above the kneecap. Keeping the leg relaxed, gently press down through the hands toward the floor until you feel a stretch behind the knee, and hold for about three seconds before releasing. The pressure should produce a stretch, never sharp pain. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions, then switch legs.', 'none (bodyweight exercise)', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'trs1800', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/2664/view/'),
  ('371cfda2-1de6-419a-b40c-fc98fd3f7e41', 'Seated Knee Tuck', 'Abs', 'Sit on floor or mat. Place arms slightly behind you. Raise legs. Now extend your legs and pull them back.', 'none (bodyweight exercise)', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'utkb', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1105/view/'),
  ('96583e33-e643-486d-95e9-67d0d5935b05', 'Seated Pancake Good Morning', 'Glutes', '- Sit with your legs completely straight (knees locked), spread wide in a straddle position.
- Place your hands on the back of your neck.
- Hinge your torso and head towards the floor.', 'none (bodyweight exercise)', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'Croak6728', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1845/view/'),
  ('ad5653e4-098e-4a84-af5b-a9349b108555', 'Seated Piriformis Stretch', null, 'Seated Piriformis Stretch
Part of: Limber 11
Source: Joe DeFranco
Prescription: 20-30 sec each side
Type: static
Includes isometric hold.', 'none (bodyweight exercise)', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'Pete-E automation', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1959/view/'),
  ('c302fd80-ce74-4202-9eee-30834872cffb', 'Seated rear delt rise', 'Lats', 'Seated, bent 45 deg forward. Arms fully stretched out, raise arms up to shoulder height and back down', 'Dumbbell', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'philip', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1098/view/'),
  ('9bcc7b4f-4172-4db7-be95-d7b659c486f5', 'Seated Row (Machine)', 'Lats', 'Keep your chest up and squeeze your shoulder blades at the end.
Don’t hunch forward or round your back during the pull.', null, 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'barry', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1725/view/'),
  ('d75ca41a-9f7d-48e5-9199-8c4b09669803', 'Seated Row (Machine) (Custom)', 'Lats', 'Perform Seated Row (Machine) with controlled form, keeping tension on the target muscles, pausing briefly at the peak contraction, then returning slowly under control without using momentum.', null, 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'ruochenma', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/2720/view/'),
  ('a00b852c-0d2b-4b4a-bbc2-ef538f211b6c', 'Seated Shoulder Extension Stretch', 'Lats, Chest', '- Sit with your hands behind you, shoulder width apart.
- Lock your elbows.
- Scoot your feet and hips out forwards, lowering your shoulders down towards ground.
- Go as far as possible to obtain a good stretch.
See the video: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ihUAbG0e8zw', 'none (bodyweight exercise)', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'Croak6728', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1841/view/'),
  ('cc5bf1a3-29b5-4c5a-8600-5e35c79ab4bf', 'Seated Triceps Press', 'Triceps', 'Sit down on a back (better with back support). Take a dumbbell firmly with both hands and hold it with extended arms over your head. With your palms facing upward and holding the weight of the dumbbell, slowly lower the weight behind your head.', 'Bench, Dumbbell', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'richmr2174@gmail.com', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/549/view/'),
  ('b2ca4a13-6fe2-4c4f-85b2-dcb5af28d2be', 'Seated V-Grip Row', 'Lats, Trapezius', 'The Seated V-Grip Row is a compound pulling exercise performed on a cable machine using a close-grip "V" handle. While seated with your feet braced, you pull the handle toward your midsection, focusing on back thickness and mid-back development.', 'Cable machine', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'amaesc', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1928/view/'),
  ('ecc46519-94b8-4ecc-b5b8-973e753e98a6', 'Seated W Curl', 'Biceps, Brachialis', '- Sit on bench with 60° incline
- Hold dumbbells beside body near the ground, palms facing outwards, arms fully extended
- Move dumbbells up using only biceps and without momentum', 'Bench, Dumbbell', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'M9', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1448/view/'),
  ('7936d8ad-6a39-4459-aa60-3e1e325f5e2b', 'Serratus Wall Slide Stretch', 'Serratus anterior', '- Stand facing a wall. Place your forearms vertically against the wall so your elbows and wrists are both touching it.
- Point your arms slightly outwards from "straight up".
- Protract your shoulders hard, then slide your forearms up the wall until your elbows are about level with your chin.
- Slide your forearms back down the wall. Repeat as necessary.', null, 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'Croak6728', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/2523/view/'),
  ('ceb58be5-2927-48c5-bb2d-4cc42b0a60e2', 'Shinbox IR Stretch', 'Glutes, Obliquus externus abdominis', '- Starting Position: Sit on the floor with both hips and knees bent at 90-degree angles.
- Leg Placement:
Place one leg in front of you (external rotation) and the other leg out
to the side/behind you (internal rotation). The shins and knees should
remain flat on the ground.
- The Movement:
Keeping your hips square, hinge your torso forward or tilt it laterally
(side-to-side) toward the front leg to deepen the stretch.
- Target Areas:
Stretches the glutes and piriformis (front leg) and the hip flexors and
quads (back leg). Engages the core and obliques during lateral flexion.
- Goal: Improves hip mobility, specifically internal and external rotation, and relieves lower back tension.', 'none (bodyweight exercise)', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'teus_ergaster', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1884/view/'),
  ('169896b2-90e3-4497-9d73-56bee4a34697', 'Shotgun Row', 'Lats', '- Attach a single handle to a low cable.
- After selecting the correct weight, stand a couple feet back with a wide-split stance. Your arm should be extended and your shoulder forward. This will be your starting position.
- Perform the movement by retracting the shoulder and flexing the elbow. As you pull, supinate the wrist, turning the palm upward as you go.
- After a brief pause, return to the starting position.', 'Cable machine', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'cal.zabel', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/562/view/'),
  ('664ddd40-a595-420d-801f-148e4bf0594c', 'Shoulder dislocates', null, 'Starting position:
Stand up with your back straight and a resistance band, towel, or broomstick handle in hand. With your hands straight in front of your body and the band between your hands, push your hands apart to both be at around 45 degrees from your body, thumbs facing down. If using a towel or broomstick handle instead, grab it with an overhand grip.
Steps:
- Keeping your arms outstretched, rotate at the shoulders to bring your arms overhead and then down toward your glutes.
- Rotate at the shoulders in the opposite direction — overhead and then toward your groin.
- Repeat.', null, 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'tinman', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1081/view/'),
  ('e237611c-2730-4d0c-891b-bb29d3d15297', 'Shoulder Dumbbell Pendular Exercise', 'Shoulders, Lats, Chest, Trapezius', '- Lean forward to rest your hand on a chair or other object, holding a dumbbell in the other hand
- Gently swing the dumbbell in a circular motion', 'Dumbbell', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'Croak6728', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1714/view/'),
  ('b283cd47-9a1c-4004-9bf5-220560ef0a16', 'Shoulder External Rotation (Cable)', 'Shoulders', 'Keep elbow fixed at your side and rotate forearm outward smoothly.
Don’t let your wrist or elbow drift upward — stay in one plane.', 'Cable machine', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'barry', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1729/view/'),
  ('2eead109-098e-4c59-bdef-f580a6a82748', 'Shoulder External Rotation with Dumbbell', 'Shoulders, Brachialis', '- Lie on your side holding a dumbbell in your upper hand
- Tuck your elbow into your side and rest the hand in front of you
- Rotate the shoulder so the hand raises up
- Lower the hand down', 'Dumbbell', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'Croak6728', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1715/view/'),
  ('19d652c4-0d94-4a33-a5b6-ab86e2d95dbc', 'Shoulder Flexion Wall Stretch', 'Lats', 'Place both hands against a wall above shoulder height. Step back and gently move the chest downward while reaching the arms overhead, keeping the back controlled. Hold a comfortable shoulder flexion stretch without forcing the range or arching the lower back.', 'none (bodyweight exercise)', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'Original exercise instructions prepared for nalhilal', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/2693/view/'),
  ('dadecc94-6322-4c66-93b5-9cb44ec79e46', 'Shoulder Internal Rotation (Cable)', 'Shoulders', 'Keep your elbow tucked to your side like it''s superglued there.
Don’t rotate your torso — only your forearm should move.', 'Cable machine', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'barry', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1728/view/'),
  ('8b0a0371-c0a9-42a7-aab7-68d520542fb2', 'Shoulder Press, Barbell', 'Shoulders', 'Sit on a bench, the back rest should be almost vertical. Take a barbell with a shoulder wide grip and bring it up to chest height. Press the weight up, but don''t stretch the arms completely. Go slowly down and repeat.', 'Barbell', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 3', 'wger.de', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/566/view/'),
  ('87affa4b-395b-437c-9581-2bd20ea5aa7c', 'Shoulder Press, Dumbbells', 'Shoulders', 'Sit on a bench, the back rest should be almost vertical. Take two dumbbells and bring them up to shoulder height, the palms and the elbows point during the whole exercise to the front. Press the weights up, at the highest point they come very near but don''t touch. Go slowly down and repeat.', 'Dumbbell', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 3', 'wger.de', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/567/view/'),
  ('5912d7ed-6a0e-4b4c-b30a-fc9f3f890fc1', 'Shoulder Press, on Machine', 'Shoulders', null, null, 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 3', 'wger.de', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/543/view/'),
  ('4a86e225-a0fb-4c83-959d-9725267a54c3', 'Shoulder Press, on Machine (Custom)', 'Shoulders', 'Perform Shoulder Press, on Machine with controlled form, keeping tension on the target muscles, pausing briefly at the peak contraction, then returning slowly under control without using momentum.', null, 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'ruochenma', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/2711/view/'),
  ('141bc870-56be-4749-a3b9-e56d5d5618b4', 'Shoulder Press, on Multi Press', 'Shoulders', 'The exercise is basically the same as with a free barbell:
Sit on a bench, the back rest should be almost vertical. Take a bar with a shoulder wide grip and bring it down to chest height. Press the weight up, but don''t stretch the arms completely. Go slowly down and repeat.', null, 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 3', 'wger.de', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/569/view/'),
  ('9a644b0e-8691-4216-b2cc-f058f58ec96d', 'Shoulder Raise (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', '- Engage the muscles
- Don''t use momentum
- Controlled movement
- Slow movement
- Always keep the arms bent
- Don''t overextend', 'Dumbbell', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'Anastasious', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1338/view/'),
  ('c146fa3c-35a4-4e6e-9000-e12a9ee19cbd', 'Shoulder Raise Side and Front DB', 'Shoulders', '- Stand while holding dumbbells beside body
- Keep arms almost fully extended
- Without momentum raise dumbbells to the side of your body until shoulder height, palms facing down
- Lower dumbbells beside body, palms facing inwards
- Immediately raise dumbbells in front of your body until shoulder height, palms facing down
- Down again
- This is one repetition', 'Dumbbell', 'wger', 'CC-BY-SA 4', 'M9', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/1443/view/'),
  ('f956977e-cc05-4db2-a387-ba6140b1ef34', 'Shoulder Shrug', 'Trapezius', 'The shoulder shrug (usually called simply the shrug) is an exercise in weight training used to develop the upper trapezius muscle. The lifter stands erect, hands about shoulder width apart, and raises the shoulders as high as possible, and then lowers them, while not bending the elbows, or moving the body at all. The lifter may not have as large a range of motion as in a normal shrug done for active flexibility. It is usually considered good form if the slope of the shoulders is horizontal in the elevated position.', 'none (bodyweight exercise)', 'wger', 'CC0', 'BFad07', 'https://wger.de/en/exercise/570/view/')
on conflict do nothing;

